# Byteman rules for row_cache_size-setRowCacheCapacityInMB-capacity--autonomous, cluster re-run (case-file amendment
# 2026-10-27 (after run 1, authorised by the user) — B3d). Observation only: each rule calls a recording method of the
# helper RcsLedger (RcsLedger.java), which never changes OHC's arguments, results or control flow.
# Loaded on every node start of the re-run with
#   JVM_EXTRA_OPTS="-javaagent:<byteman jar>=script:<this file>,boot:<byteman jar>,sys:<rcs-ledger.jar>"
#
# ohc-core 0.5.1, org.caffinitas.ohc.linked.Uns:
#   allocated(long address, long bytes)  :104-113, called by allocate(long, boolean) :338-346 only after a non-zero malloc
#   freed(long address)                  :90-102,  called by free(long) :361-367 for a non-zero address, before allocator.free
# Every native block OHC's linked implementation takes or returns passes through these two methods (all Uns.allocate /
# Uns.free call sites, OHCacheLinkedImpl, OffHeapLinkedMap, HashEntries, Timeouts, the channel classes).

RULE rcs ledger allocated
CLASS org.caffinitas.ohc.linked.Uns
METHOD allocated(long, long)
HELPER RcsLedger
AT ENTRY
IF true
DO alloc($1, $2)
ENDRULE

RULE rcs ledger freed
CLASS org.caffinitas.ohc.linked.Uns
METHOD freed(long)
HELPER RcsLedger
AT ENTRY
IF true
DO free($1)
ENDRULE
